The Opportunity &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Uniting the expertise and capabilities of Ashfield and Huntsworth Health, Inizio has just been launched to become THE strategic partner for health and life sciences companies. Unparalleled in scale and expertise, we connect a full suite of Advisory, Medical, Marketing/Communications, Patient and Stakeholder Engagement, and Biotech services to reimagine clients' business challenges into opportunities.&nbsp; &nbsp;

&nbsp;

We are a team of 12,000 experts working together in 35 countries to create something extraordinary. We exist to solve health challenges and develop transformational ideas that positively impact human lives. Working at Inizio offers an opportunity to work for a game-changing company built with one goal. That is to redefine health and life sciences by empowering our people to inspire new possibilities that advance health and build brighter futures. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Role &nbsp;

&nbsp;

As a Compensation Analyst, you will be responsible for supporting the day-to-day administration and delivery of compensation programs and processes across the business. Reporting to the Service Delivery Senior Manager - TComp and Leaves of Absence, you will play a key role in ensuring compensation transactions, annual compensation cycles, reporting, and system processes are completed accurately, efficiently, and in accordance with established policies and controls. Working closely with the Total Rewards team and other key stakeholders, you will help maintain compensation data integrity, provide operational support to HR colleagues and managers, and identify opportunities to improve processes and the overall service experience. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Here’s What You’ll Be Doing &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Annual Compensation Cycle Operations &nbsp;

• Support the administration and execution of annual merit and bonus cycles, ensuring activities are completed accurately and within established timelines. &nbsp;

• Assist with compensation cycle preparation, including eligibility reviews, data validation, Workday configuration, and testing. &nbsp;

• Provide operational guidance and support to HR colleagues and people managers throughout compensation planning cycles. &nbsp;

• Monitor compensation submissions, approval workflows, and completion of required activities. &nbsp;

• Validate final compensation outcomes and coordinate payroll outputs and reconciliation to ensure accurate processing. &nbsp;

• Identify and resolve discrepancies, escalating complex issues to the appropriate stakeholders. &nbsp;

Job and Market Data Operations &nbsp;

• Support compensation benchmarking activities, including salary survey participation, data collection, and submissions. &nbsp;

• Maintain compensation benchmarking databases and support job matching and market data reviews. &nbsp;

• Assist with the maintenance of salary ranges, job grades, and compensation structures. &nbsp;

• Support the accuracy and consistency of job architecture and related compensation data. &nbsp;

• Provide data and analysis to support compensation reviews and recommendations developed by the Total Rewards team. &nbsp;

Compensation Data and Reporting &nbsp;

• Prepare and maintain standard compensation reports, dashboards, and audit reports. &nbsp;

• Analyze compensation data to identify discrepancies, trends, and opportunities for improvement. &nbsp;

• Support the preparation of pay equity and pay-gap datasets, ensuring data accuracy and completeness. &nbsp;

• Respond to ad hoc compensation data requests from HR, Finance, and Total Rewards stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Review and validate compensation requests to ensure alignment with established policies, guidelines, and approval requirements.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Support standard offer compensation validation and preparation of compensation-related letters and documentation. &nbsp;

